# Defend The City — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development, and set the same
# values in the Vercel dashboard (Settings → Environment Variables) for
# production. `.env.local` is gitignored; never commit real values.
#
# Every variable here is OPTIONAL. With none of them set, the game runs
# fully — you just get no leaderboard, no feedback form, and no analytics.
# That's deliberate: a fresh clone should be playable immediately.
#
# The VITE_ prefix is what makes Vite expose a variable to browser code.
# It also means these values are PUBLIC — they ship inside the JS bundle.
# Only ever put publishable keys here. Supabase's `service_role` key must
# never appear in this file or anywhere else in this repo.

# --- Supabase (leaderboard + feedback) -------------------------------
# Dashboard → Project Settings → API. Use the "anon / public" key.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- PostHog (analytics) ---------------------------------------------
# Dashboard → Settings → Project → Project API Key (starts with "phc_").
VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=
# US cloud (default if unset): https://us.i.posthog.com
# EU cloud:                    https://eu.i.posthog.com
# Getting this wrong means events silently go nowhere, so set it
# explicitly if your project is in the EU region.
VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com
